IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `comp50-nouns`
IMPORT `comp50-cross-references`

-- Row il-50. The controls agree with themselves, the recorded facts about the three defects are what NOTES.md says they are, and the days the two halves of a date pair answer differently are NOTHING.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their six failing assertions are in comp50-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in comp50-cross-references.l4 and from the calendar routine's output, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- Each control pair names the same day in both halves.
#ASSERT `the printed pair agrees` (`control: Fees Regulations, the Minister's signature line`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`control: Fees Regulations, the Minister's signature line`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the printed pair agrees` (`control: Fees Regulations, the running date line of the issue`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`control: Fees Regulations, the running date line of the issue`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the printed pair agrees` (`control: Compromise Regulations, the Minister's signature line`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`control: Compromise Regulations, the Minister's signature line`) EQUALS 0
-- The control of defect 4 names the same day in both halves.
#ASSERT `the printed pair agrees` (`control: KT 7639, the signature lines of 10 Adar II 5776`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`control: KT 7639, the signature lines of 10 Adar II 5776`) EQUALS 0
-- Neither saved Ordinance section of the controls shares a number with what the later law cancels.
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`control keeps: Ordinance s 33`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance ss 195 to 201`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`control keeps: Ordinance s 33`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`control keeps: Ordinance s 115א`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance ss 195 to 201`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`control keeps: Ordinance s 115א`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`) EQUALS 0

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- The pairs of the two defects: the page image was read; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
#ASSERT (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- The pairs of the controls: the page image was read, and no later instrument is in question.
#ASSERT (`control: Fees Regulations, the Minister's signature line`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`control: Fees Regulations, the running date line of the issue`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`control: Compromise Regulations, the Minister's signature line`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
-- The five signature lines of defect 4: the first was read from the page image; the other four, and the control, in the text layer only.
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 2 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on notice of a general meeting`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the text layer of the official instrument, not the page image`
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 3 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on how long a resolution is valid`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the text layer of the official instrument, not the page image`
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 4 of 5, p. 949, the regulations on outside directors who are not Israeli residents`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the text layer of the official instrument, not the page image`
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 5 of 5, p. 949, the order changing the First Schedule A to the Law`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the text layer of the official instrument, not the page image`
#ASSERT (`control: KT 7639, the signature lines of 10 Adar II 5776`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the text layer of the official instrument, not the page image`
-- The saving clause is the consolidation only; the cancelled sections 195 to 201 are read from the page image; where the cancelled chapters begin and end is the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 164 to 201`)'s `the ends of the run were read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 244 to 367`)'s `the ends of the run were read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 370 to 382`)'s `the ends of the run were read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`the later law cancels: Ordinance ss 195 to 201`)'s `the ends of the run were read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`)'s `the ends of the run were read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`

§ `Tests of what the two halves of the date pairs say`

-- DEFECT 1. The Hebrew half and the Gregorian half name different days, 29 days apart. The printed Gregorian day is before the issue date printed at the foot of the same pages (control 2); the Hebrew half's day is after it.
#ASSERT NOT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the earlier of the two days` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) EQUALS (Date 1 1 2001)
#ASSERT `the later of the two days` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) EQUALS (Date 30 1 2001)
#ASSERT (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`)'s `the Gregorian day as printed` AT MOST (`control: Fees Regulations, the running date line of the issue`)'s `the Gregorian day as printed`
#ASSERT NOT ((`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`)'s `the Gregorian day the Hebrew date computes to` AT MOST (`control: Fees Regulations, the running date line of the issue`)'s `the Gregorian day as printed`)
-- DEFECT 2. The two halves name days 366 days apart (the span includes 29 February 2008).
#ASSERT NOT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) EQUALS 366
#ASSERT `the earlier of the two days` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) EQUALS (Date 15 7 2007)
#ASSERT `the later of the two days` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) EQUALS (Date 15 7 2008)
-- DEFECT 4. All five signature lines print the same pair, "25 Adar I 5776" with 8 March 2016, and in each the two halves are 3 days apart: the Hebrew half computes to 5 March 2016.
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`)'s `the Hebrew date as printed` EQUALS "25 Adar I 5776"
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`)'s `the Gregorian day as printed` EQUALS (Date 8 3 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 2 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on notice of a general meeting`)'s `the Hebrew date as printed` EQUALS "25 Adar I 5776"
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 2 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on notice of a general meeting`)'s `the Gregorian day as printed` EQUALS (Date 8 3 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 2 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on notice of a general meeting`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 2 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on notice of a general meeting`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 3 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on how long a resolution is valid`)'s `the Hebrew date as printed` EQUALS "25 Adar I 5776"
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 3 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on how long a resolution is valid`)'s `the Gregorian day as printed` EQUALS (Date 8 3 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 3 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on how long a resolution is valid`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 3 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on how long a resolution is valid`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 4 of 5, p. 949, the regulations on outside directors who are not Israeli residents`)'s `the Hebrew date as printed` EQUALS "25 Adar I 5776"
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 4 of 5, p. 949, the regulations on outside directors who are not Israeli residents`)'s `the Gregorian day as printed` EQUALS (Date 8 3 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 4 of 5, p. 949, the regulations on outside directors who are not Israeli residents`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 4 of 5, p. 949, the regulations on outside directors who are not Israeli residents`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 5 of 5, p. 949, the order changing the First Schedule A to the Law`)'s `the Hebrew date as printed` EQUALS "25 Adar I 5776"
#ASSERT (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 5 of 5, p. 949, the order changing the First Schedule A to the Law`)'s `the Gregorian day as printed` EQUALS (Date 8 3 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 5 of 5, p. 949, the order changing the First Schedule A to the Law`)
#ASSERT `the days between the two days` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 5 of 5, p. 949, the order changing the First Schedule A to the Law`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the earlier of the two days` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`) EQUALS (Date 5 3 2016)
#ASSERT `the later of the two days` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`) EQUALS (Date 8 3 2016)
-- DEFECT 3. The saving clause's three runs hold 38, 124 and 13 numbers; the cancelled sections hold 7 and the cancelled chapters, as the consolidation places them, 139.
#ASSERT `how many numbers a run holds` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 164 to 201`) EQUALS 38
#ASSERT `how many numbers a run holds` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 244 to 367`) EQUALS 124
#ASSERT `how many numbers a run holds` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 370 to 382`) EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `how many numbers a run holds` (`the later law cancels: Ordinance ss 195 to 201`) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `how many numbers a run holds` (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`) EQUALS 139
-- The overlaps, run against run: the first range shares its last 7 numbers with the cancelled sections 195 to 201 and none with the chapters; the second and third ranges lie wholly inside the cancelled chapters.
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 164 to 201`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance ss 195 to 201`) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 164 to 201`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 244 to 367`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance ss 195 to 201`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 244 to 367`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`) EQUALS 124
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 370 to 382`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`) EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 244 to 367`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`) EQUALS `how many numbers a run holds` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 244 to 367`)
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 370 to 382`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`) EQUALS `how many numbers a run holds` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 370 to 382`)

§ `Tests of the days the two halves answer differently`

-- DEFECT 1: regulations in force from the day. A day before both printed days is FALSE, a day on or after both is TRUE, and the days from 1 January to 29 January 2001 are NOTHING: the text does not say which half governs (fork F1).
#ASSERT `the regulations are in force on` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) (Date 31 12 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the regulations are in force on` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) (Date 1 1 2001) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the regulations are in force on` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) (Date 15 1 2001) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the regulations are in force on` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) (Date 29 1 2001) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the regulations are in force on` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) (Date 30 1 2001) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the regulations are in force on` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- DEFECT 2: a temporary provision in force until a day. A day before both printed days is TRUE and a day after both is FALSE. Each printed day, and every day between them, is NOTHING (forks F1 and F2).
#ASSERT `the temporary provision is in force on` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) (Date 1 1 2007) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the temporary provision is in force on` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) (Date 14 7 2007) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the temporary provision is in force on` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) (Date 15 7 2007) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the temporary provision is in force on` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) (Date 1 1 2008) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the temporary provision is in force on` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) (Date 15 7 2008) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the temporary provision is in force on` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) (Date 16 7 2008) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the temporary provision is in force on` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
